  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of ICT services to the humanitarian actors in Pulka and Damboa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThe ETS, as a standard service sector, provides reliable internet and security communications services to the entire humanitarian community including UN agencies, and local and international NGOs. The ETS services remains vital to the humanitarian actor as it helps to ensure the safety and security of humanitarian actors working in high-risk regions in the BAY states.&#xA0;ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtA joint assessment was conducted in Damboa to assess ICT service needs by ETS, IOM and UNDSS include partner NGOs working in Damboa. Following this joint assessment, the ETS will,ltspangt&#xA0;Deploy ICT services in Damboa and Pulka. The services include Internet connectivity services and Security communications services to ensure safety and security of the humanitarian actors on field.lt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
